          "guid": "mspivhh6dsanwav2",
          "message": {
            "text": "Mirror Blink’s post-MapCharacters style conversion before returning the native fallback face. Chromium’s FontDescription::UpdateFromSkiaFontStyle preserves only Skia OBLIQUE and converts Skia ITALIC to normal; native diagnostics proved DirectWrite nominated style=2 italic for U+A700/U+1DF00 while Chrome painted the reopened regular Segoe UI/Calibri cuts. Coverage is intentionally checked after reopening because Blink rejects a reopened family cut that lacks the codepoint.",
            "markdown": "Mirror Blink’s post-MapCharacters style conversion before returning the native fallback face. Chromium’s FontDescription::UpdateFromSkiaFontStyle preserves only Skia OBLIQUE and converts Skia ITALIC to normal; native diagnostics proved DirectWrite nominated style=2 italic for U+A700/U+1DF00 while Chrome painted the reopened regular Segoe UI/Calibri cuts. Coverage is intentionally checked after reopening because Blink rejects a reopened family cut that lacks the codepoint."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tools/win32-glyph-extractor/src/main.cpp"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1178,
                  "endLine": 1214,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "        // `family` query with that converted style before testing coverage.\n        // This is what turns DirectWrite's Calibri-Italic / SegoeUI-Italic\n        // nominations for the DM-2083 probes into Chrome's regular cuts.\n        if (!familyName.empty()) {\n          std::wstring mappedFamilyW = toWide(familyName);\n          UINT32 familyIndex = 0;\n          BOOL familyExists = FALSE;\n          if (SUCCEEDED(systemFonts->FindFamilyName(mappedFamilyW.c_str(), &familyIndex,\n                                                     &familyExists)) && familyExists) {\n            IDWriteFontFamily* mappedFamily = nullptr;\n            if (SUCCEEDED(systemFonts->GetFontFamily(familyIndex, &mappedFamily)) && mappedFamily) {\n              IDWriteFont* reopened = nullptr;\n              const DWRITE_FONT_STYLE blinkSlant =\n                  mappedFont->GetStyle() == DWRITE_FONT_STYLE_OBLIQUE\n                    ? DWRITE_FONT_STYLE_OBLIQUE\n                    : DWRITE_FONT_STYLE_NORMAL;\n              if (SUCCEEDED(firstMatchingFontWithoutSimulations(\n                      mappedFamily, mappedFont->GetWeight(), mappedFont->GetStretch(),\n                      blinkSlant, &reopened)) && reopened) {\n                safeRelease(mappedFont);\n                mappedFont = reopened;\n              }\n              safeRelease(mappedFamily);\n            }\n          }\n        }\n        BOOL covers = FALSE;\n        // Coverage guard: only report a face that actually has the glyph.\n        if (SUCCEEDED(mappedFont->HasCharacter(cp, &covers)) && covers) {\n          IDWriteFontFace* face = nullptr;\n          if (SUCCEEDED(mappedFont->CreateFontFace(&face)) && face) {\n            psName = facePostScriptName(face);\n            path = fontFacePath(face);\n            familyName = fontFamilyDisplayName(mappedFont);\n            axesJson = faceResolvedAxesJson(face);  // DM-1721: variable-instance axis pin\n            if (!psName.empty() && !path.empty()) found = true;\n            safeRelease(face);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
